{{!
    @template mod_rememberme/session_choices

    A single response multiple choice question, presented as a hand of options
    the learner clicks. There is no submit button: the click is the answer.

    The same markup carries the question and its verdict, because the verdict is
    a state of the options rather than a separate screen. The letter on each
    option becomes a tick or a cross in place, so the result is never carried by
    colour alone.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * data-action="choose" on each option
    * data-name and data-value on each option

    Context variables required for this template:
    * name String The response field name the answer is submitted under
    * questiontext String The question, already formatted
    * graded Boolean Whether the answer is in
    * verdict String The result, shown once graded
    * choices Array The options
        * value Number The value to submit
        * text String The option, already formatted
        * token String The letter, or the verdict mark once graded
        * isright Boolean Whether this is the right answer
        * iswrong Boolean Whether this is the wrong answer the learner chose
        * isfaded Boolean Whether this option is no longer in play

    Example context (json):
    {
        "name": "q1:1_answer",
        "questiontext": "<p>Which planet is closest to the Sun?</p>",
        "graded": true,
        "verdict": "Not quite",
        "choices": [
            {"value": 0, "text": "Mercury", "token": "✓", "isright": true, "iswrong": false, "isfaded": false},
            {"value": 1, "text": "Earth", "token": "✕", "isright": false, "iswrong": true, "isfaded": false},
            {"value": 2, "text": "Venus", "token": "C", "isright": false, "iswrong": false, "isfaded": true}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="rmm-hand">
    <div class="rmm-prompt">{{{questiontext}}}</div>

    {{#choices}}
        <button type="button"
                class="rmm-choice{{#isright}} is-right{{/isright}}{{#iswrong}} is-wrong{{/iswrong}}{{#isfaded}} is-faded{{/isfaded}}"
                data-action="choose" data-name="{{name}}" data-value="{{value}}"
                {{#graded}}disabled{{/graded}}>
            <span class="rmm-token" aria-hidden="true">{{token}}</span>
            <span class="rmm-choice-text">{{{text}}}</span>
        </button>
    {{/choices}}

    {{#graded}}
        <p class="rmm-verdict">{{verdict}}</p>
    {{/graded}}
</div>
